{"id":8665,"date":"2024-05-25T07:00:00","date_gmt":"2024-05-25T07:00:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/?p=8665"},"modified":"2025-09-05T16:11:10","modified_gmt":"2025-09-05T16:11:10","slug":"5-construction-industry-terminology-you-cant-afford-to-miss","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/5-construction-industry-terminology-you-cant-afford-to-miss\/","title":{"rendered":"5 Construction Industry Terminology You Can&#8217;t Afford To Miss"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;<em>5 Construction Industry Terminology You Can&#8217;t Afford to Miss<\/em>&#8220;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Understanding key construction terms is crucial whether you&#8217;re a seasoned professional or new to the industry. Here, we explore five essential construction industry terms, explaining what they mean and how they affect your job prospects. With this knowledge, you&#8217;ll be better equipped to navigate the construction process and communicate effectively with colleagues and clients. And if at any stage of construction you need expert assistance, <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/\" title=\"\">Harris &amp; Sons<\/a> is ready to help. Let&#8217;s dive into these must-know construction jargon terms.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/industry-details-construction-site-yellow-bulld-2023-11-27-05-08-19-utc-1024x684.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-8669\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Subcontractor<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Role and Responsibilities<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A subcontractor is a specialist hired by a general contractor to perform specific tasks within a larger project. Subcontractors do not own the project&#8217;s equipment or materials and typically focus on one particular trade, such as electrical work, plumbing, or carpentry. They must coordinate closely with the general contractor and other subcontractors to ensure their part of the project is completed on time and to specification.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Finding Reliable Subcontractors<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Choosing the right subcontractor is critical for the success of any construction project. In places like Happy Valley, OR or Tigard, OR, look for subcontractors with proven experience, strong references, and the necessary licenses and insurance. Websites, industry forums, and local trade associations can be invaluable resources for finding and vetting reliable subcontractors.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Subcontractor Management<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Effective management of subcontractors involves clear communication of project expectations, regular progress checks, and prompt payment for services rendered. Understanding subcontractor agreements and ensuring they are detailed and legally sound can help prevent disputes and ensure smooth project progression.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Project Manager<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Role and Responsibilities<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A project manager is responsible for overseeing the entire construction project from start to finish. This includes the planning, execution, monitoring, controlling, and closing phases. Project managers ensure that the project stays on schedule, within budget, and meets quality standards. They coordinate with the client, general contractor, subcontractors, and suppliers to keep everything running smoothly.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Qualifications and Skills<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Key qualifications for a project manager typically include a background in construction management or engineering, strong organizational skills, and excellent communication abilities. Certifications such as PMP (Project Management Professional) can enhance a project manager&#8217;s credentials and job prospects.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Project Management in Action<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a bustling construction site in places like Beaverton, OR, or Happy Valley, OR, or Gresham, OR, the project manager&#8217;s role is indispensable. They are the hub of all project activities, ensuring that every phase transitions smoothly into the next and that any issues are addressed promptly.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/project-manager-and-construction-worker-looking-at-2023-11-27-05-00-15-utc-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-8671\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">General Contractor<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Role and Responsibilities<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A general contractor (GC) is responsible for the day-to-day oversight of the construction site, management of vendors and trades, and communication of information to all involved parties throughout the course of a building project. The GC hires and manages subcontractors, procures materials, and ensures compliance with building codes and standards.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">General Contractor vs. Subcontractor<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While both general contractors and subcontractors are essential to a construction project, their roles differ significantly. The GC oversees the entire project, whereas subcontractors focus on specific tasks. Understanding this distinction is vital when hiring professionals for your project.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Choosing a General Contractor<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Selecting a competent GC in areas like Happy Valley, OR, or Clackamas, OR, involves reviewing their previous work, checking licenses and insurance, and confirming their ability to handle projects similar to yours. Recommendations and reviews from previous clients can also provide insight into their reliability and quality of work.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Building Code<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Understanding Building Codes<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Building codes are a set of regulations that specify the standards for constructed objects such as buildings and non-building structures. These codes ensure that buildings are safe, healthy, and accessible. They cover aspects like structural integrity, fire safety, energy efficiency, and accessibility.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Compliance and Permits<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Before starting any construction project, understanding and adhering to local building codes is essential. This involves obtaining the necessary permits, which vary by state and municipality. For example, requirements in Hillsboro, OR, might differ significantly from those in Battleground, WA.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Importance of Building Codes<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Adhering to building codes is not only a legal requirement but also a safety measure that protects the well-being of the occupants and the longevity of the structure. Non-compliance can lead to fines, legal issues, and unsafe living conditions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/05\/building-construction-industry-2023-11-27-05-23-05-utc-1024x684.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-8672\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Architectural Design<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Role in Construction<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Architectural design involves creating the plans and specifications for a building project. This process includes determining the layout, materials, and overall aesthetic of the building. Architects must balance functionality, safety, and aesthetics to create structures that meet the needs of their clients.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Permits and Approvals<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Before construction begins, the architectural design must be approved by the relevant authorities. This includes obtaining a building permit, which verifies that the design complies with local building codes and regulations. In cities like Lake Oswego, OR, and Happy Valley, OR the approval process can include multiple stages of review.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Impact on Construction<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The architectural design sets the tone for the entire construction process. It guides the work of contractors and subcontractors, ensuring that everyone is working towards the same vision. High-quality architectural plans can prevent misunderstandings and mistakes during construction, leading to a smoother and more efficient project.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is the role of a subcontractor in construction?<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A subcontractor specializes in a specific trade within a construction project, such as electrical work or plumbing. They work under the direction of a general contractor.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How does a project manager differ from a general contractor?<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> A project manager oversees the planning and execution of the entire project, focusing on timelines and budgets. A general contractor manages the day-to-day operations on the construction site and coordinates subcontractors.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What are building codes and why are they important?<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> Building codes are regulations that ensure the safety, health, and accessibility of buildings. Compliance with building codes is crucial for legal and safety reasons.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why is architectural design important in construction?<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> Architectural design provides the plans and specifications for a construction project, balancing functionality, safety, and aesthetics. It guides the work of all involved parties.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How do I find reliable subcontractors and general contractors?<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> Seek recommendations from trusted sources, review credentials and past work, and check for necessary licenses and insurance. Local trade associations and online resources can also be helpful.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Conclusion<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Understanding these key construction industry terms\u2014subcontractor, project manager, general contractor, building code, and architectural design\u2014is essential for anyone involved in the building industry. Whether you&#8217;re in Beaverton, OR, or Happy Valley, OR remember that if at any stage of construction you need expert assistance, <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/services\/\" title=\"\">Harris &amp; Sons<\/a> is ready to help. We are prepared to become your construction colleague and solve complex problems quickly and professionally.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>&#8220;5 Construction Industry Terminology You Can&#8217;t Afford to Miss&#8220; Understanding key construction terms is crucial whether you&#8217;re a seasoned professional or new to the industry. Here, we explore five essential construction industry terms, explaining what they mean and how they affect your job prospects. With this knowledge, you&#8217;ll be better equipped to navigate the construction [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":8668,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[31,33],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-8665","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-contractors-guides","category-remodeling-tips"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/8665","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=8665"}],"version-history":[{"count":4,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/8665\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13694,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/8665\/revisions\/13694"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=8665"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=8665"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=8665"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}